System Architecture : 
----------------------

Frontend (UI or simple API client)
        ↓
Backend API Service
        ↓
Database (stateful)



Service we must build : 
-----------------------


1. Frontend Service (optional simple API client)

Can be Node/Python simple service
Calls backend service

2. Backend Service (IMPORTANT)
This is your Phase 1 app upgraded
Must now:
Store and retrieve data from DB
Use environment-based config
Fail gracefully when DB is down

Endpoints:

/health
/config
/data → writes/reads from DB


3.Database (Stateful)

Pick ONE:

PostgreSQL (recommended)
OR
MongoDB

You MUST deploy it as:
StatefulSet OR managed external DB (your choice, but justify it)


New Kubernetes Concepts you must use: 

1.Ingress Controller

Use:

NGINX Ingress OR AWS ALB Ingress (if EKS)
This is your first real traffic routing layer.

2.Persistent Storage
PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)
Storage class awareness

Database MUST NOT lose data on restart.

3.Environment Separation
You must simulate:

* dev namespace
* staging namespace

Same app, different configs.


